<h1>BA combined recovery + interpolation QC</h1><p>Skim the path, inspect anything odd, and record a decision. A quick skim is not full-video validation. Recommendations do not remove data.</p>
<header><label>Reviewer <input id="reviewer" placeholder="Your name" size="12"></label><a href="REVIEW_WORKFLOW.html" target="_blank">Saving and returning reviews</a><button id="export">Download ALL QC scores</button><button id="csv">Download summary CSV</button><label>Import QC JSON <input id="import" type="file" accept=".json"></label><span id="progress"></span><small>A approve · T turtling reject · R reject · F needs review. Shortcuts are inactive while typing. Download ALL QC scores before leaving; browser saves are local, not yet in the registry.</small></header>
<div class="layout"><aside><input id="search" placeholder="Search run or recording" aria-label="Search runs"><select id="filter" aria-label="Filter runs"><option value="all">All runs · QC order</option><option value="unreviewed">Not yet skimmed</option><option value="flagged">Flagged (including approved)</option><option value="usable_skim">Approved / looks usable</option></select><div id="gallery" class="gallery"></div></aside>
<main><section class="panel quickDecision" aria-label="Quick review decisions"><div class="quickHeading"><b id="quickRun"></b><b id="turtlePercent"></b></div><div class="toolbar"><button id="usable" class="good">Approve for analysis [A] · save & next</button><button id="flag">Needs review [F] · save & next</button><button id="turtleReject" class="turtleAction">Reject: turtling [T]</button><button id="reviseLast">Revise last decision</button><button id="exclude" class="bad">Reject / exclude [R] · save & next</button></div><div id="flags" class="flags"></div><fieldset><legend>What did you inspect?</legend><span id="scope"><label><input type="radio" name="coverage" value="trace_skim" checked> Trace skim</label> <label><input type="radio" name="coverage" value="trace_and_excerpt"> Trace + short video</label> <label><input type="radio" name="coverage" value="trace_and_full_video"> Trace + full video</label></span></fieldset><small>Check concerns and approve if usable. T adds the possible-turtling reason and recommends exclusion; nothing is deleted. <label><input id="shortcuts" type="checkbox" checked> Keyboard shortcuts on</label></small><b id="saved"></b><p id="msg" role="status"></p><details><summary>Percentage details</summary><small id="turtlePercentDetail"></small></details></section><div class="panel"><div class="toolbar"><button id="prev">Previous</button><button id="next">Next</button><button id="nextOpen">Next unreviewed</button><b id="title"></b></div><div id="label"></div><p id="metrics"></p><details><summary>Tracking and detector details</summary><small id="auto"></small><p id="versionNote"></p><p id="turtleStatus" style="color:#9238b1;font-weight:bold"></p><small> Purple: automatic frozen 0.4 screening on recovery before interpolation; pink: human possible-turtling intervals. No flag does not prove upright posture. Interpolated frames are not assessed.</small><p id="strictStatus" style="color:#a53716;font-weight:bold"></p><button id="nextJump">Inspect next flagged jump</button><small> Starts a short video excerpt around each jump. Approval alone does not release movement statistics; the explicit human override below does.</small></details></div>
<div class="panel"><div class="views"><section><div class="toolbar"><label><input type="checkbox" id="raw"> Original tracking</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="pro"> Recovery before interpolation</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="strict" checked> Strict final track</label></div><canvas id="trace" width="500" height="500" aria-label="Full spatial trajectory"></canvas><p class="legend">Default teal: strict final track, with unresolved jump endpoints unknown; orange: interpolation; purple: automatic turtling; pink: human turtling flags. Recovery is distinguished in coordinate exports. Originals are retained for comparison. Missing positions break traces. Click a path point to inspect its time.</p></section><section><div class="videoWrap"><video id="video" playsinline preload="metadata"></video><canvas id="overlay" width="500" height="500" aria-label="Proposed position circle and recent path"></canvas></div><small id="overlayStatus"></small><div class="toolbar"><label><input id="overlayOn" type="checkbox" checked> Circle + recent path</label></div><small>Teal: selected track · blue: recovery · orange: interpolation · gray: optional raw comparison. Video trails never connect ≥100 px jumps. Circle follows the proposal, not a confirmed beetle position.</small><b id="frame"></b><div class="toolbar"><button id="play">Play / pause</button><button id="back">−1 frame</button><button id="forward">+1 frame</button><select id="speed" aria-label="Playback speed"><option value="1">1×</option><option value="2">2×</option><option value="4">4×</option><option value="0.5">0.5×</option></select></div><input id="seek" type="range" step="1" aria-label="Global video frame"><div class="toolbar"><button id="excerpt">Play 10 s around here</button><button id="full">Play full run</button><label>Frame <input id="goto" type="number" size="8" style="width:110px"></label><button id="go">Go</button></div><small id="mediaStatus"></small></section></div>
<canvas id="timeplot" width="1100" height="130" aria-label="Adjacent step size and missing tracking over time"></canvas><small>Click timeline to seek. Gray step trace; red bars: jumps; amber: interpolation; orange-red: missing tracking; brown: brightness changes; dark gray: human-excluded frames; purple: automatic turtling; pink: your turtling flags. Step height is capped at 200 px for display.</small><div id="events"></div><details><summary>Earlier attributed review notes</summary><div id="prior"></div></details></div>
<div class="panel"><h2 style="font-size:19px">Review details and annotations</h2><small>Flags are retained for filtering and do not prevent approval. Approve for analysis keeps your selected concerns in the possible_flags output column. Automatic movement holds still need the explicit override.</small><label>Suggest removal above <input id="turtleCutoff" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="0.1" placeholder="Not set" style="width:110px"> % turtled (all runs)</label><b id="turtleCutoffStatus"></b><p><small>Estimate combines automatic candidates and your completed bouts, counting overlaps once, divided by all frames in this run. Unmarked or unassessed frames are not confirmed upright. The cutoff flags review only; it does not exclude a run.</small></p><p><label><input id="rerun" type="checkbox"> Request IDTracker rerun</label> <small>Records a request only; no job is submitted.</small></p><p><label><input id="movementOverride" type="checkbox"> Human override: allow movement analysis despite jump flags</label><br><small>Use the strict track: flagged endpoints remain missing; no movement is credited across gaps. Save with Approve for analysis. Your name and review scope are recorded.</small></p><textarea id="notes" rows="2" placeholder="Optional detail: where the trace looks wrong, why exclude, what might help fix it"></textarea><div class="toolbar"><button id="turtleStart">Mark turtling start</button><button id="turtleEnd">Mark turtling end</button><button id="turtleClear">Clear turtling intervals</button><span id="turtleRanges"></span><button id="markStart">Mark issue start here</button><button id="markEnd">Mark issue end here</button><button id="clearRanges">Clear optional intervals</button><span id="ranges"></span></div><small>Intervals are optional QC locations, not posture scores or tracking exclusions.</small><small>Saved locally in this browser. Download JSON to preserve decisions and reviewer history. Unreviewed runs remain unreviewed. Exclusion recommendations require a separate downstream inclusion decision.</small></div></main></div>
